---
import Deck from "../layouts/Deck.astro";
import Slide from "../components/Slide.astro";
import Globe from "../components/Globe.astro";
import PlanetSlide from "../components/PlanetSlide.astro";
import Chapter from "../components/Chapter.astro";
import Lineup from "../components/Lineup.astro";
import Orrery from "../components/Orrery.astro";
import LightRace from "../components/LightRace.astro";
import { planets } from "../data/planets";

const by = Object.fromEntries(planets.map((p) => [p.id, p]));
const right = { size: 1100, x: 1400, y: 540 };
const left = { size: 1100, x: 520, y: 540 };
---

<Deck title="The Solar System">
  <Slide id="title" layout="title" class="title">
    <div class="backdrop">
      <Globe body="sun" width={1920} height={1080} radius={430} cx={1500} cy={560} style="position:absolute;left:0;top:0" />
    </div>
    <p class="kicker">A grand tour · One star · Eight worlds</p>
    <h1>The Solar<br /><em class="sun-text">System</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">4.6 billion years of rocks, ice and gas falling around a very ordinary star.</p>
    <Fragment slot="notes">
      <p>Every body in this deck is drawn live by one fragment shader: no textures, no images. The starfield is generated at build time by an Astro endpoint.</p>
      <p>Press <strong>O</strong> for the overview, <strong>P</strong> for presenter view.</p>
    </Fragment>
  </Slide>

  <Slide id="mass" layout="center" class="mass">
    <div class="backdrop"><div class="corona"></div></div>
    <p class="kicker">Gravitational budget</p>
    <p class="big sun-text">99.86%</p>
    <p class="lede">of all the mass in the Solar System is the Sun.</p>
    <p class="muted rest" data-step data-effect="rise">Jupiter is most of the rest. Earth is a rounding error.</p>
    <Fragment slot="notes">
      <p>The other 0.14% is mostly Jupiter (about 0.1%). All the rocky planets together: about 0.0006%.</p>
    </Fragment>
  </Slide>

  <Slide id="scale" class="scale">
    <Lineup />
    <header>
      <p class="kicker">Everything, to scale</p>
      <h2>Mind the <em>gap</em></h2>
      <p class="lede">Line up 109 Earths and you have crossed the face of the Sun once.</p>
    </header>
    <Fragment slot="notes">
      <p>Diameters to scale; distances are not. At this scale Neptune would sit 60 km to the right.</p>
      <p>Step 1 names the rocky planets, step 2 the giants.</p>
    </Fragment>
  </Slide>

  <Slide id="orrery" class="orrery" steps={1}>
    <Orrery />
    <header>
      <p class="kicker">Live, from above</p>
      <h2>Where everyone <em>is</em></h2>
      <p class="lede">Starting today and running fast. Next zooms out to Neptune.</p>
    </header>
    <Fragment slot="notes">
      <p>Positions come from each planet's mean longitude at J2000 plus its mean motion: circular orbits, but the right planets in the right places today.</p>
      <p>Distances use a square-root scale. The asteroid belt is 1,800 particles obeying Kepler's third law. The speed buttons don't advance the deck.</p>
    </Fragment>
  </Slide>

  <Chapter id="inner" part="Part I" highlight={["mercury", "venus", "earth", "mars"]} reach={1.65} glow="#ff7a2f" row={320}>
    <Fragment slot="title">The <em>inner</em><br />worlds</Fragment>
    Small, dense and rocky: forged where the young Sun burned off everything light.
  </Chapter>

  <PlanetSlide planet={by.mercury} group="Inner worlds" globe={right}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>Bump-mapped craters from three octaves of Worley cells. The bump fades near the limb, where screen-space derivatives get blocky.</p></Fragment>
  </PlanetSlide>
  <PlanetSlide planet={by.venus} group="Inner worlds" globe={left} flip>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>We only ever see the cloud tops. They super-rotate: the atmosphere laps the planet every four days.</p></Fragment>
  </PlanetSlide>
  <PlanetSlide planet={by.earth} group="Inner worlds" globe={right} phase={30}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>Continents, ice caps, ocean glint, drifting clouds and city lights on the night side. All procedural, so not <em>our</em> continents.</p></Fragment>
  </PlanetSlide>
  <PlanetSlide planet={by.mars} group="Inner worlds" globe={left} flip>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>Two moons, Phobos and Deimos, probably captured asteroids.</p></Fragment>
  </PlanetSlide>

  <Chapter id="giants" part="Part II" highlight={["jupiter", "saturn", "uranus", "neptune"]} reach={31} glow="#4f6bff">
    <Fragment slot="title">The <em>giants</em></Fragment>
    Past the frost line there was ice to build with, and the planets grew enormous.
  </Chapter>

  <PlanetSlide planet={by.jupiter} group="Giants" globe={right}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>The Great Red Spot drifts into view while the slide is up.</p></Fragment>
  </PlanetSlide>
  <PlanetSlide planet={by.saturn} group="Giants" globe={{ size: 1500, x: 500, y: 540 }} flip>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>The rings cast the planet's shadow and the planet casts the rings' shadow: two ray–plane tests in the shader. Cassini division and Encke gap included.</p></Fragment>
  </PlanetSlide>
  <PlanetSlide planet={by.uranus} group="Giants" globe={right}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>Its faint rings run almost pole to pole because the whole system is tipped over.</p></Fragment>
  </PlanetSlide>
  <PlanetSlide planet={by.neptune} group="Giants" globe={left} flip>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>Urbain Le Verrier predicted Neptune's position from wobbles in Uranus's orbit; Galle found it within a degree in 1846.</p></Fragment>
  </PlanetSlide>

  <Slide id="light" class="light">
    <LightRace />
    <header>
      <p class="kicker">At 299,792 km/s</p>
      <h2>Sunlight's <em>commute</em></h2>
      <p class="lede">The light reaching Neptune right now left the Sun four hours ago.</p>
    </header>
    <Fragment slot="notes">
      <p>The track is logarithmic past Mercury: the photon moves at constant speed while the clock speeds up exponentially. Replay with the button.</p>
    </Fragment>
  </Slide>

  <Slide id="pale-blue-dot" layout="quote" class="pbd" transition="warp">
    <div class="backdrop">
      <div class="beams">
        <i style="--x:58%;--w:110px;--c:#c98a5c;--o:0.28"></i>
        <i style="--x:66%;--w:70px;--c:#a07ad0;--o:0.2"></i>
        <i style="--x:73%;--w:160px;--c:#e9b88f;--o:0.32"></i>
        <i style="--x:84%;--w:90px;--c:#6f8fd8;--o:0.2"></i>
      </div>
      <span class="dot"></span>
      <span class="ring" data-step data-effect="rise">You are here</span>
    </div>
    <blockquote>Look again at that dot. That's here. That's home. That's us.</blockquote>
    <cite>Carl Sagan, <em>Pale Blue Dot</em>, 1994</cite>
    <Fragment slot="notes">
      <p>Voyager 1 took the photo on 14 February 1990 from six billion kilometres away. Earth is less than a pixel, caught in a ray of scattered sunlight.</p>
    </Fragment>
  </Slide>

  <Slide id="thanks" layout="center" class="thanks" transition="warp">
    <div class="backdrop">
      <Globe body="earth" width={1920} height={560} radius={1600} cx={960} cy={1820} light="top" phase={12} style="position:absolute;left:0;bottom:0" />
    </div>
    <h1>Clear <em>skies</em></h1>
    <p class="muted">Astro · @slides/deck · one fragment shader · <code>demos/astro</code></p>
  </Slide>
</Deck>

<style>
  .title {
    gap: 40px;
  }
  .title h1 {
    font-size: 250px;
    line-height: 0.82;
    margin-left: -10px;
  }
  .title h1 em {
    display: inline-block;
    padding-right: 0.08em;
  }
  .title .lede {
    max-width: 18ch;
  }

  .mass .corona {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse 60% 50% at 50% 50%, rgb(255 138 61 / 0.16), transparent 70%);
  }
  .mass .big {
    position: relative;
    font: 400 380px/0.9 var(--deck-font-heading);
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 0 60px rgb(255 140 50 / 0.45));
  }
  .mass .lede {
    position: relative;
    max-width: none;
  }
  .mass .rest {
    position: relative;
    font-size: 32px;
  }

  :is(.scale, .orrery, .light) header {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
    max-width: 900px;
  }
  .scale header {
    margin-left: 360px;
  }
  .scale header h2,
  .orrery header h2,
  .light header h2 {
    font-size: 120px;
  }
  .orrery header .lede {
    font-size: 32px;
    max-width: 20ch;
  }
  .scale header .lede,
  .light header .lede {
    font-size: 34px;
    max-width: 28ch;
  }

  .pbd {
    padding-right: 900px;
  }
  .pbd blockquote {
    position: relative;
    font: italic 400 96px/1.05 var(--deck-font-heading);
  }
  .pbd blockquote::before {
    color: #8fb4ff;
  }
  .pbd cite {
    position: relative;
    font-size: 30px;
  }
  .beams i {
    position: absolute;
    top: -20%;
    left: var(--x);
    width: var(--w);
    height: 140%;
    rotate: 14deg;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--c), transparent);
    opacity: var(--o);
    filter: blur(14px);
  }
  .pbd .dot {
    position: absolute;
    left: 1460px;
    top: 612px;
    width: 5px;
    height: 5px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #bcd4ff;
    box-shadow: 0 0 8px 2px rgb(150 190 255 / 0.7);
  }
  .pbd .ring {
    position: absolute;
    left: 1432px;
    top: 584px;
    width: 60px;
    height: 60px;
    border: 1.5px solid rgb(188 212 255 / 0.7);
    border-radius: 50%;
    font: 500 18px/1 var(--deck-font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #bcd4ff;
    white-space: nowrap;
    text-indent: 80px;
    line-height: 60px;
  }

  .thanks {
    justify-content: flex-start;
    padding-top: 200px;
  }
  .thanks h1 {
    position: relative;
    font-size: 220px;
  }
  .thanks p {
    position: relative;
    font-size: 30px;
  }
</style>
